2,"uses":2},{"base":"H1775","lemma":"דִּימוֹן","tr":"di·mon","gloss":"Dibon","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":2},{"base":"H3215","lemma":"יְלָלָה","tr":"ye·la·lah","gloss":"wailing","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":5},{"base":"H1820","lemma":"דָּמָה","tr":"da·mah","gloss":"to cease","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":15},{"base":"H2201","lemma":"זְעָקָה","tr":"ze·a·qah","gloss":"outcry","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":18},{"base":"H3213","lemma":"יָלַל","tr":"ya·lal","gloss":"to wail","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":30},{"base":"H7703","lemma":"שָׁדַד","tr":"sha·dad","gloss":"to ruin","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":57},{"base":"H2199","lemma":"זָעַק","tr":"za·aq","gloss":"to cry out","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":73}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"AMO","chapter":2,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"This is what the LORD says: “For three transgressions of Moab, even four, I will not revoke My judgment, because he burned to lime the bones of Edomʼs king.","from":1},{"book":"AMO","chapter":2,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"I will cut off the ruler of Moab and kill all the officials with him,” says the LORD.","from":1},{"book":"2KI","chapter":17,"verse":25,"verseEnd":25,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Now when the settlers first lived there, they did not worship the LORD, so He sent lions among them, which killed some of them.","from":9},{"book":"JER","chapter":48,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"Concerning Moab, this is what the LORD of Hosts, the God of Israel, says: “Woe to Nebo, for it will be devastated. Kiriathaim will be captured and disgraced; the fortress will be shattered and dismantled.","from":1},{"book":"JER","chapter":48,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"For on the ascent to Luhith they weep bitterly as they go, and on the descent to Horonaim cries of distress resound over the destruction:","from":5},{"book":"JER","chapter":48,"verse":47,"verseEnd":47,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"Yet in the latter days I will restore Moab from captivity,” declares the LORD. Here ends the judgment on Moab.","from":1},{"book":"GEN","chapter":13,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And Lot looked out and saw that the whole plain of the Jordan, all the way to Zoar, was well watered like the garden of the Lord, like the land of Egypt. (This was before the Lorddestroyed Sodom and Gomorrah.)","from":5},{"book":"GEN","chapter":14,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"went to war against Bera king of Sodom, Birsha king of Gomorrah, Shinab king of Admah, Shemeber king of Zeboiim, and the king of Bela (that is, Zoar).","from":5}],"notes":[],"groups":[]}}